    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Asystole is the complete absence of cardiac electrical activity - a flat line on the ECG monitor. Like PEA, it is a NON-SHOCKABLE rhythm. Asystole carries the worst prognosis of all cardiac arrest rhythms & typically represents a terminal event, but reversible -> must always be systematically sought."
     }
    ]
   },
